----- stdout -----
Command line interface for gameready

Usage: gameready [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init        Set up this machine: find your games, pick which to tune, apply
  doctor      Report system facts and what each step would do
  explain     Say what a step does, why, and what it would change on this machine
  list-games  List the game profiles gameready can see, and where each came from
  apply       Apply improvements
  rollback    Undo a previous run
  selftest    Apply a step, verify it, roll it back, and verify it reverted
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json                   Print the run report as JSON instead of a rendered summary
      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>  Write the state directory somewhere else. Used by tests to keep runs
                               out of the invoking user's real journal [env:
                               GAMEREADY_STATE_DIR=[TMP]
      --games-dir <GAMES_DIR>  Read your own game profiles from somewhere other than
                               `~/.config/gameready/games` [env:
                               GAMEREADY_GAMES_DIR=[TMP]
  -h, --help                   Print help
  -V, --version                Print version

